// The requirements of the language as a DAG (SREQ-00012-1): the purpose at
// the root, then the domains of the language, then the entities, then one
// requirement per characteristic; the rules that hold for every instance of
// a category are constraints, hung where they apply. Nesting is refinement.
// Every leaf names the oracle test that fixes it, and the member of ds that
// implements it realises it. The grammar box holds the rules of the text
// (grammar/grammar.ds). This file knows nothing of who consumes the language:
// the connections to the system's SREQ live in design/wiring.ds, the
// consumer's file (decided 2026-10-26).

package driftspec@ds {

  requirement REQ-00012-1 {
    tags: language
    status: approved
    verification VER-00048-1 {
      status: approved
      title: Unit tests confirm every oracle corpus of the language means what it marks
      method: test
      tests:
        tests/integration/ds/check/test_static.cpp::TestStatic.TheOracleFindingsAndNothingElse
        tests/integration/ds/check/test_behaviour.cpp::TestBehaviour.TheOracleFindings
        tests/integration/ds/check/test_artefacts.cpp::TestArtefacts.TheOracleFindingsAndNothingElse
    }
    title: The language shall specify a software design as text: its high-level design, its low-level design, the artefacts about it and the views of it
    rationale:
      One text, one meaning, for the whole of a design: what the tool loads,
      checks, draws, compares and asks about.

    // ======================= metamodel ====================================
    requirement REQ-00066-1 {
      tags: language, metamodel
      status: approved
      title: The language shall be declared once as a metamodel: every kind with its fields, flags and parents, every relation with the kinds it joins
      text:
        Each kind names the fields it carries, each with a type (text, name,
        names, type, params, number, status, patterns) and who sets it (the
        author, the syntax, or the checker), the flags it takes and the kinds
        it may be declared inside; a field whose name ends in * is a family
        (local.*, exit *, contract.*). Each relation names the kinds it may go
        from and to. Everything the binder and the checker put in a model is
        something the metamodel declares.
      rationale:
        Owner, 2026-11-05: DriftSpec has its own data model, not argos's. The
        binder wrote some fifty field names that nothing declared, and every
        reader parsed them again; the render of the whole model (DS-67) needs
        to know what exists before drawing it.
      verification VER-00072-3 {
        status: approved
        title: Integration tests confirm that the design of ds and every example corpus are made only of what the metamodel declares, a relation the language does not allow is reported and not bound, and the metamodel places each kind where the grammar does and declares every flag the binder sets
        method: test
        tests:
          tests/integration/ds/check/test_conformance.cpp::TestMetamodelConformance.EveryEntityAndRelationIsOneTheMetamodelDeclares
          tests/integration/ds/check/test_conformance.cpp::TestMetamodelConformance.ARelationTheLanguageDoesNotAllowIsReportedAndNotBound
          tests/integration/ds/model/test_metamodel_truth.cpp::TestMetamodelTruth.EveryKindIsDeclaredInWhatTheGrammarLetsItBeWrittenIn
          tests/integration/ds/model/test_metamodel_truth.cpp::TestMetamodelTruth.EveryFlagTheBinderSetsIsOneItsKindDeclares
      }
      verification VER-00075-1 {
        status: approved
        title: Integration tests confirm parameters and arguments are read once into structures that agree with their text, over the design of ds and every example
        method: test
        tests:
          tests/integration/ds/check/test_conformance.cpp::TestMetamodelConformance.ParametersAndArgumentsAreReadOnceAndAgreeWithTheirText
      }
      requirement REQ-00067-1 {
        tags: language, metamodel, fields
        status: approved
        title: A field that its kind does not declare shall be reported as W-FIELD-UNKNOWN
        text:
          A key: value an entity carries that the metamodel does not declare
          for its kind (a typo, or a field the language does not know) is a
          warning at the entity, naming the field and the kind. It is kept in
          the model: the warning does not drop it.
        rationale:
          DS-22: a misspelt field entered silently. The metamodel now says
          which fields exist, so the checker can say which do not.
        verification VER-00073-1 {
          status: approved
          title: Integration tests confirm an undeclared field is reported and a declared one is not, and the diag corpus marks its layout field
          method: test
          tests:
            tests/integration/ds/check/test_conformance.cpp::TestMetamodelConformance.AFieldItsKindDoesNotDeclareIsReportedAndADeclaredOneIsNot
        }
      }

      requirement REQ-00115-1 {
        tags: language, metamodel, fields
        status: approved
        title: A closed field carrying a value it does not take shall be reported as W-FIELD-VALUE
        text:
          The metamodel names the values of its closed fields: status (draft,
          approved, obsolete), a verification's method and level, a diagram's
          kind and level. Any other value is a warning at the entity, naming the
          field, the value and the values it takes; an empty value is left alone.
          The value is kept in the model.
        rationale:
          Model audit 2026-11, findings G4 and G3 (DS-211): status: aproved
          passed, stopped counting as approved and so switched
          W-REQ-NO-VERIFICATION off; kind: clas fell back to a class diagram and
          level: package was ignored in silence.
        verification VER-00131-1 {
          status: approved
          title: Integration tests confirm a closed field with a value it does not take is reported and one it takes is not, and the diag corpus marks a component kind
          method: test
          tests:
            tests/integration/ds/check/test_conformance.cpp::TestMetamodelConformance.AClosedFieldWithAValueItDoesNotTakeIsReportedAndOneItTakesIsNot
        }
      }
    }

    // ======================= workspace ====================================
    requirement REQ-00053-1 {
      tags: language, workspace
      status: approved
      title: A specification shall be a directory of .ds files read as one, in any order
      text:
        Files are read whole and are not units of meaning; a reference nobody
        declares is an expected node reported once (W-REF-UNDECLARED) and never
        stops the load; only syntax stops a file (E-SYNTAX).
      rationale:
        A specification that lives per file cannot say that two files talk
        about the same thing (R1, R6).
      verification VER-00041-2 {
        title: Integration tests confirm a specification is a directory of .ds files read as one, in any order
        status: approved
        method: test
        tests:
          tests/integration/ds/check/test_checker.cpp::TestChecker.UndeclaredReferencesBecomeExpectedNodesReportedOnce
          tests/integration/ds/parse/test_workspace_parsing.cpp::TestWorkspaceParsing.TheFilesOfADirectoryAreReadAsOneInAnyOrder
          tests/integration/ds/parse/test_workspace_parsing.cpp::TestWorkspaceParsing.AFileThatParsesReportsNoSyntaxErrorBesideOneThatDoesNot
      }
      constraint CST-00002-1 {
        tags: language, workspace
        status: approved
        category: language
        title: Every entity shall have one identity, and a second declaration of it shall be E-DUPLICATE-IDENTITY
        rationale: R5: identity across the workspace is what makes references, diagrams and diffs mean the same entity everywhere.
      }
      constraint CST-00003-2 {
        tags: language, workspace
        status: approved
        category: language
        title: Every entity shall be defined once and extended only by blocks of annotations
        text:
          An extension adds relations and never touches the definition; an extension of nothing is an expected node,
          except a class: written with annotations only and defined by no other block, it is the class, empty, and its
          scope contains it (revision 2, DS-20: an exception class that only carries its requirements).
        rationale: A box writes its requirements without knowing who consumes them (2026-10-26).
      }
    }

    // ======================= HLD ==========================================
    requirement REQ-00013-1 {
      tags: language, hld
      status: approved
      verification VER-00049-1 {
        status: approved
        title: Unit tests confirm the HLD is modelled as nested packages
        method: test
        tests:
          tests/integration/ds/bind/test_packages.cpp::TestPackages.EveryPackageLevelAddsItsNameWithAt
      }
      title: The language shall model the high-level design as packages, the organisation above the implementation
      rationale:
        The HLD is where a system is divided into deployable units and
        boundaries; argos reads it as boxes that own namespaces.

      requirement REQ-00014-1 {
        tags: language, hld
        status: approved
        verification VER-00050-1 {
          status: approved
          title: Unit tests confirm a package is a box holding packages, modules and artefacts
          method: test
          tests:
            tests/integration/ds/bind/test_packages.cpp::TestPackages.TheFlatFormIsTheSameIdentityAsNesting
            tests/integration/ds/bind/test_packages.cpp::TestPackages.LevelByPlacementThroughTheLevels
        }
        title: A package shall be a box of the high-level design: a black box that holds packages, modules and artefacts
        rationale: R1, R2; nested packages 2026-10-26.

        requirement REQ-00015-1 {
          tags: language, hld
          status: approved
          title: A package shall nest in a package, written nested or reopened flat by its full path
          text:
            package app { package core { } } and package app@core { } are the
            same box; the flat form needs the outer package declared somewhere.
          verification VER-00012-1 {
            title: Integration tests confirm a package nests in a package, written nested or reopened flat by its full path
            status: approved
            method: test
            tests:
              tests/integration/ds/bind/test_packages.cpp::TestPackages.EveryPackageLevelAddsItsNameWithAt
              tests/integration/ds/bind/test_packages.cpp::TestPackages.TheFlatFormIsTheSameIdentityAsNesting
              tests/integration/ds/bind/test_packages.cpp::TestPackages.AnOuterPackageNobodyDeclaresIsExpected
          }
        }
        constraint CST-00004-1 {
          tags: language, hld
          status: approved
          category: language
          title: Every identity shall name its packages with @ and its namespaces with ::, the box that holds the modules rooting the code's namespace
          text:
            app@core@model::Entity: boxes with @, namespaces with ::; outer
            boxes are organisation and drop out of the qualified name.
          rationale: decided 2026-10-26 with argos's reading by namespace (R4).
        }
        requirement REQ-00017-2 {
          tags: language, hld
          status: approved
          title: A package or a module shall realise requirements and carry constraints through annotations, like a class
          text: @requirement and @constraint in the package or module body.
          rationale:
            Revises REQ-00017-1, which named the package only: the metamodel let
            a module answer to a requirement but the grammar did not let one
            write it (DS-82, found by a newcomer agent, 2026-11-06).
          verification VER-00014-2 {
            title: Integration tests confirm a package or a module realises requirements and carries constraints through annotations, like a class
            status: approved
            method: test
            tests:
              tests/integration/ds/bind/test_packages.cpp::TestPackages.ABoxRealisesRequirementsLikeAClass
              tests/integration/ds/bind/test_module_annotations.cpp::TestModuleAnnotations.AModuleAnswersToTheRequirementItsBodyNames
          }
        }
        requirement REQ-00084-1 {
          tags: language, hld
          status: approved
          title: A package or a module shall say what its code is written in, and what it holds shall be written in the same unless it says otherwise
          text:
            language: cpp in a package or a module; cpp, c, python, typescript or lua, the
            languages argos reads. What a box holds is written in its language unless it says
            another, and the check fills the language down, so every package and module of the
            model carries it. One ds does not know, or two at once (a reopened box that says
            two), is W-LANGUAGE-UNKNOWN. A box that says nothing and is held by nothing that
            says has no language.
          rationale:
            Owner, 2026-11-06 (DS-86): nothing said which technology each package used, and
            DriftSpec designs both C++ and Python (iris; the Python face of ds itself). Knowing
            it, argos picks the reader of each box and writes its types the way that language
            does.
          verification VER-00093-1 {
            title: Integration tests confirm a box's language is held by what it holds unless it says otherwise, and an unknown one or two at once is a finding
            status: approved
            method: test
            tests:
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_language.cpp::TestLanguage.WhatABoxHoldsIsWrittenInItsLanguageUnlessItSaysOtherwise
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_language.cpp::TestLanguage.ABoxThatSaysNothingAndHoldsNothingThatSaysHasNoLanguage
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_language.cpp::TestLanguage.ALanguageDsDoesNotKnowOrTwoAtOnceIsAFinding
          }
        }
        requirement REQ-00018-1 {
          tags: language, hld
          status: approved
          title: The outermost package shall be the system, and the level of an artefact shall follow from where it is declared
          text:
            In the outermost package an artefact is of the system; in an inner
            package or a module, of that level. No keyword, no field.
          verification VER-00015-2 {
            title: Integration tests confirm the outermost package is the system, and the level of an artefact follows from where it is declared
            status: approved
            text: Revision 2 (DS-184) cites the integration test alone; the unit test of a scope is the class's own.
            method: test
            tests:
              tests/integration/ds/bind/test_packages.cpp::TestPackages.LevelByPlacementThroughTheLevels
          }
        }
        requirement REQ-00019-1 {
          tags: language, hld
          status: approved
          title: A package shall draw as a container of its modules in a class diagram
          verification VER-00016-1 {
            title: Integration tests confirm a package draws as a container of its modules in a class diagram
            status: approved
            method: test
            tests:
              tests/integration/ds/bind/test_packages.cpp::TestPackages.NestedPackagesAreContainersOfTheDrawing
          }
        }
        requirement REQ-00020-2 {
          tags: language, hld
          status: approved
          title: A package shall declare the external interfaces of what it builds, with their kind and typed operations
          text:
            interface shell { kind: cli; operation buy(sku: string) -> int { exit 2: refused } }, at any
            level of packages. The kind and the fields of an operation are data, not grammar, so a new
            kind changes no syntax. Quality is a requirement or a constraint linked to the interface or
            to an operation. Replaces boundary (DS-54): an interface of the high level design is the
            external interface of a process, or of a library when it is binary.
          rationale: Owner, 2026-11-05. The syntax is self-contained, with no other formats or parsers.
          verification VER-00064-1 {
            title: Integration tests confirm a package declares the external interfaces of what it builds, with their kind and typed operations
            status: approved
            method: test
            tests:
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_interfaces.cpp::TestInterfaces.AnInterfaceHoldsItsTypedOperationsAndTheirFields
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_interfaces.cpp::TestInterfaces.RequirementsAndConstraintsLinkToAnInterfaceOrAnOperation
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_interfaces.cpp::TestInterfaces.AnInterfaceIsDrawnAsABoxWithItsOperations
          }
        }
        requirement REQ-00088-1 {
          tags: language, hld, dependencies
          status: approved
          title: A package, a module or a class shall declare that it uses an interface another box offers, in its own body or from another file
          text:
            @uses sistema@broker@publish in a box binds a consumes relation from the box to the interface; the
            box that offers the interface is the provider. Like every annotation it binds the same
            written in the box or in an extension block anywhere else, so the wiring of a system can
            live in a file of its own (as design/wiring.ds does for requirements) and a design brought
            in whole can be connected from above without being touched. What an annotation means is
            read from the metamodel's table of annotations, declared once.
          rationale:
            Owner, 2026-11-07 (DS-96): designing a distributed system live, the high level design could
            not say that the service uses the broker's publish interface; the boxes stood apart. The
            Owner asked for the link to be external, like the wiring of requirements.
          verification VER-00097-1 {
            title: Integration tests confirm a box uses an interface of another, written in its body or in another file, and a use of something that is no interface is reported
            status: approved
            method: test
            tests:
              tests/integration/ds/bind/test_uses.cpp::TestUses.APackageAModuleOrAClassUsesAnInterfaceOfAnotherBox
              tests/integration/ds/bind/test_uses.cpp::TestUses.AUseWrittenInAnotherFileBindsTheSame
              tests/integration/ds/bind/test_uses.cpp::TestUses.AUseOfSomethingThatIsNoInterfaceIsReportedAndNotBound
              tests/integration/ds/bind/test_uses.cpp::TestUses.AnAnnotationMeansWhatTheMetamodelSaysWhereverItIsWritten
          }
        }
        requirement REQ-00093-1 {
          tags: language, hld, dependencies
          status: approved
          title: A module shall offer interfaces like a package, and a behaviour shall call an interface's operation through a local, a parameter or an attribute typed by it
          text:
            interface port { ... } inside module face is p@face::port, offered by the module. A
            behaviour reaches an interface's operation as it reaches a method: local ds: p@engine
            then -> ds.check(text), or a parameter or an attribute typed by the interface; the call
            names the operation, so the consumer depends on the contract and not on the class that
            realises it. In the viewer a module's interfaces come first inside it.
          rationale:
            Owner, 2026-11-07 (DS-92): the Python face called the engine's class Api because a
            sequence could not call engine; and a dependency between two modules of one package had
            no interface to go through.
          verification VER-00102-1 {
            title: Integration tests confirm a module offers interfaces and a behaviour calls an interface's operation through a local, a parameter or an attribute
            status: approved
            method: test
            tests:
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_interface_calls.cpp::TestInterfaceCalls.AModuleDeclaresAnInterfaceAndOffersIt
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_interface_calls.cpp::TestInterfaceCalls.ABehaviourCallsAnInterfaceOperationThroughALocal
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_interface_calls.cpp::TestInterfaceCalls.ThroughAParameterOrAnAttributeTypedByTheInterface
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_interface_calls.cpp::TestInterfaceCalls.TheSceneDrawsAModulesInterfaceInsideIt
          }
        }
        requirement REQ-00094-2 {
          tags: language, hld, dependencies, check
          status: approved
          title: The checker shall compare what a box declares it uses with what its behaviours call, and report what is not declared, what is declared and never called, and a call that goes around an interface
          text:
            A call to an operation of an interface another box offers needs a @uses of that interface
            on the caller or on a box it lives in, written there or in a wiring file
            (W-USES-UNDECLARED). A @uses that none of the box's behaviours calls is dead, said only once
            the box has behaviours (W-USES-UNUSED). A call to a method of a class that realises an
            interface, from outside the class's module, goes around the contract when the method
            answers an operation of that interface (W-USES-BYPASS); a method the interface does not
            offer cannot be called through it and is no bypass (DS-106). An
            interface's own sequences realise it, and a box calling an interface it offers depends on
            nothing.
          rationale: Owner, 2026-11-07 (DS-96, DS-92): declared dependencies are only worth what the behaviour confirms.
          verification VER-00103-2 {
            title: Integration tests confirm undeclared, unused and bypassing dependencies are reported, and what is declared, planned or realised is not
            status: approved
            method: test
            tests:
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_dependency_checks.cpp::TestDependencyChecks.ACallToAnotherBoxsInterfaceNeedsAUseOnTheCallerOrWhereItLives
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_dependency_checks.cpp::TestDependencyChecks.AUseOnTheModuleOrInAWiringBlockOnItsPackageCoversTheCall
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_dependency_checks.cpp::TestDependencyChecks.AUseNoBehaviourCallsIsDeadOnceTheBoxHasBehaviours
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_dependency_checks.cpp::TestDependencyChecks.CallingTheClassBehindAnInterfaceFromOutsideGoesAroundIt
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_dependency_checks.cpp::TestDependencyChecks.AnInterfacesOwnSequenceRealisesItAndNothingIsReported
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_dependency_checks.cpp::TestDependencyChecks.AMethodTheInterfaceDoesNotOfferIsNoBypass
          }
        }
        requirement REQ-00119-1 {
          tags: language, hld, interfaces, check
          status: approved
          title: A method that answers an operation of an interface its class realises shall take and give what the operation does, or be reported as W-INTERFACE-SIGNATURE
          text:
            When a class realises an interface (@interface) and declares, or inherits, a method named
            like one of the interface's operations, their parameters and returns are compared as the
            idea each type commits to: qualifiers dropped, std::vector read as the neutral list, void
            as none. A difference is a warning at the method. An operation the class does not declare
            is no finding: that is absence.
          rationale:
            Model audit 2026-11, finding G5 (DS-215): a class realising keeper declared feed(animal:
            int, extra: bool) against feed(animal: string) and nothing was said, while between an
            operation and its use case the signatures were compared. It is the link from the
            high-level design to the low-level one.
          verification VER-00135-1 {
            title: Integration tests confirm a method that answers an interface operation with another signature is reported, one that says the same idea is not, and an operation the class does not declare is no finding
            status: approved
            method: test
            tests:
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_dependency_checks.cpp::TestRealisation.AMethodThatAnswersAnInterfaceOperationWithAnotherSignatureIsReported
          }
        }
        requirement REQ-00081-1 {
          tags: language, hld, usecase
          status: approved
          title: A use case shall be declared as a contract with its outcomes, realised by interface operations and specialised by a specific use case
          text:
            usecase UC-00001-1 greet(name: string) -> Greeting { outcome default: ...; outcome
            empty-name -> none: ... } is an artefact identified by its id with its revision: a
            title, a status, the requirements that bind it (@requirement), an optional signature
            and its outcomes, default the ending that goes well and every other one a scenario.
            It names no interface: an interface operation realises it (operation greet(...) :
            UC-00001-1), whoever drives that interface. A specific use case specialises a
            generic one after a colon and keeps its signature, its outcomes and its
            requirements. A design without use cases owes none.
          rationale:
            Owner, 2026-11-06 (DS-77): a use case is its own entity, close to a requirement; it
            may be bound by several requirements and triggered from several interfaces of the
            high level design, and it should be seen whole from each of them. No actor: the
            interface already says what drives it.
          verification VER-00090-1 {
            title: Integration tests confirm hola realises its use cases from both interfaces, a specific one inherits the outcomes of its generic, and a design without use cases owes none
            status: approved
            method: test
            tests:
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_usecases.cpp::TestUseCases.HolaRealisesItsUseCasesFromBothInterfacesAndChecksClean
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_usecases.cpp::TestUseCases.ASpecificUseCaseInheritsTheOutcomesOfItsGeneric
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_usecases.cpp::TestUseCases.ADesignWithoutUseCasesOwesNone
          }
        }
        requirement REQ-00082-1 {
          tags: language, hld, usecase, check
          status: approved
          title: The check shall hold every operation that realises a use case to its contract, outcome by outcome
          text:
            An operation that takes or gives something else than the use case it realises, or a
            specific use case that does so against its generic, is W-USECASE-SIGNATURE. An
            outcome, its own or inherited, that the operation handles with no scenario is
            W-USECASE-OUTCOME-UNHANDLED; a scenario the operation handles that no outcome names
            is W-SCENARIO-NO-OUTCOME. A use case no operation realises, directly or through one
            that specialises it, is W-USECASE-UNREALISED; a realisation or a specialisation of an
            id that is no use case is W-USECASE-UNDECLARED.
          rationale:
            The use case is what makes "from which interfaces, and how does it end" checkable:
            on ds's own design these checks caught the outcomes the command line changed.
          verification VER-00091-1 {
            title: Integration tests confirm each way an operation can break its use case is a finding, and keeping the contract is none
            status: approved
            method: test
            tests:
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_usecases.cpp::TestUseCases.AnOperationThatHandlesEveryOutcomeKeepsTheContract
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_usecases.cpp::TestUseCases.AnOperationThatGivesSomethingElseBreaksTheContract
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_usecases.cpp::TestUseCases.AnOutcomeNoScenarioHandlesIsReported
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_usecases.cpp::TestUseCases.AScenarioNoOutcomeNamesIsReported
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_usecases.cpp::TestUseCases.AUseCaseNothingRealisesAndAnUnknownOneAreReported
          }
        }
      }
    }

    // ======================= LLD ==========================================
    requirement REQ-00021-1 {
      tags: language, lld
      status: approved
      verification VER-00051-1 {
        status: approved
        title: Unit tests confirm the LLD is modelled as modules of classes and behaviours: the static oracle
        method: test
        tests:
          tests/integration/ds/check/test_static.cpp::TestStatic.TheOracleFindingsAndNothingElse
      }
      title: The language shall model the low-level design as modules of classes and their behaviours
      rationale: The white box: what argos compares with the code.

      // ---- module ----
      requirement REQ-00022-1 {
        tags: language, lld, module
        status: approved
        verification VER-00052-1 {
          status: approved
          title: Unit tests confirm a module is a namespace that reopens
          method: test
          tests:
            tests/integration/ds/bind/test_binder.cpp::TestBinder.ModulesCanBeReopenedAcrossFilesButClassesCannot
        }
        title: A module shall be a namespace that reopens across files and resolves names outward
        rationale: R2, R9, R10.

        requirement REQ-00023-1 {
          tags: language, lld, module
          status: approved
          title: A bare name shall resolve from the innermost scope outward, a qualified name across modules, a pkg@ one across packages
          text: No includes, no using; what already encloses you is omitted.
          verification VER-00017-1 {
            title: Integration tests confirm a bare name resolves from the innermost scope outward, a qualified name across modules, a pkg@ one across packages
            status: approved
            method: test
            tests:
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_checker.cpp::TestChecker.ResolvesInnermostScopeFirst
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_static.cpp::TestStatic.CrossModuleReferencesNeedTheModuleNotAnInclude
              tests/integration/ds/bind/test_binder.cpp::TestBinder.ModulesCanBeReopenedAcrossFilesButClassesCannot
          }
        }
        requirement REQ-00024-2 {
          tags: language, lld, module
          status: approved
          title: An extern module shall declare names only, with no obligations, and every extern shall join one catalogue
          text:
            A bare name nobody declares in scope resolves to the one extern
            of that simple name, whatever the template arguments of the use
            or of the declaration (tuple<int, str> finds class tuple);
            among several of that name, the one of the use's arity wins,
            and two left without a winner make it E-REF-AMBIGUOUS. The type
            text stays as written.
          rationale:
            R11; the catalogue 2026-10-26. Revision 2: an extern's template
            arguments are not the design's to check, and a generic used by
            its bare name never found its extern (tuple<2> against class
            tuple), which left every generic Python type of the iris spike
            undeclared.
          verification VER-00018-2 {
            title: Integration tests confirm an extern module declares names only, with no obligations, and every extern joins one catalogue
            status: approved
            method: test
            tests:
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_static.cpp::TestStatic.ExternDeclaresIdentitiesWithoutObligations
              tests/integration/ds/bind/test_packages.cpp::TestPackages.ABareNameFallsBackToTheExternCatalogue
              tests/integration/ds/bind/test_packages.cpp::TestPackages.AGenericUseFindsTheExternOfItsSimpleName
          }
        }
      }

      // ---- class ----
      requirement REQ-00025-1 {
        tags: language, lld, class
        status: approved
        verification VER-00053-1 {
          status: approved
          title: Unit tests confirm classes, dataclasses and enums have identities and members
          method: test
          tests:
            tests/integration/ds/check/test_static.cpp::TestStatic.EnumsAndTemplatesHaveIdentities
            tests/integration/ds/check/test_static.cpp::TestStatic.DefaultsAndModifiersAreKept
        }
        title: A class shall be a type of the design: class, dataclass or enum, with members
        rationale: R12, R14, R19.

        requirement REQ-00026-1 {
          tags: language, lld, class
          status: approved
          title: A member shall carry visibility, modifiers, a name, a type and an optional default
          text:
            + # -, then abstract | static | const for methods or owns | refs |
            shares for attributes, then the name; a method named like its
            class is a constructor; name: type = default. Members are
            identified by name: an overload is one member.
          verification VER-00019-1 {
            title: Integration tests confirm a member carries visibility, modifiers, a name, a type and an optional default
            status: approved
            method: test
            tests:
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_static.cpp::TestStatic.DefaultsAndModifiersAreKept
          }
        }
        constraint CST-00005-1 {
          tags: language, lld, class
          status: approved
          category: language
          title: Every modifier shall be a word only in front of a name: nothing is reserved
          text: + abstract: bool is an attribute named abstract.
          rationale: decided 2026-10-26: a code base designed in DriftSpec keeps its names.
        }
        requirement REQ-00028-1 {
          tags: language, lld, class
          status: approved
          title: Ownership and multiplicity shall come from the attribute and its type; parameters and returns shall give use
          text:
            owns (default), refs, shares; T is 1, optional<T> 0..1, list, set,
            vector, map are *, a qualified container the same, and a container
            passes the relation to its element. E-OWNERSHIP-CYCLE,
            W-MODIFIER-ON-VALUE.
          rationale: R16.
          verification VER-00021-2 {
            title: Integration tests confirm ownership and multiplicity come from the attribute and its type, and parameters and returns give use
            status: approved
            method: test
            tests:
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_static.cpp::TestStatic.OwnershipAndMultiplicityComeFromTheAttribute
              tests/integration/ds/render/test_irexport.cpp::TestIrExport.AnEnumIsAValueSoItIsAssociatedNotOwned
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_type_reading.cpp::TestTypeReading.AQualifiedContainerHandsTheCallToItsElement
          }
        }
        requirement REQ-00029-1 {
          tags: language, lld, class
          status: approved
          title: A template shall be identified by name and arity and its arguments checked against their bounds
          text: class Repository<T: Entity>; E-TEMPLATE-BOUND.
          rationale: R15.
          verification VER-00022-2 {
            title: Integration tests confirm a template is identified by name and arity and its arguments checked against their bounds
            status: approved
            method: test
            tests:
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_static.cpp::TestStatic.EnumsAndTemplatesHaveIdentities
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_type_reading.cpp::TestTypeReading.ATemplatesArityCountsItsOwnArgumentsOnly
          }
        }
        requirement REQ-00030-1 {
          tags: language, lld, class
          status: approved
          title: Operators shall be declared in the class header as a set and refined in the body
          text: class Vector <<==, ordered, +, []>>; E-OPERATOR-UNDECLARED.
          rationale: R17.
          verification VER-00023-1 {
            title: Integration tests confirm operators are declared in the class header as a set and refined in the body
            status: approved
            method: test
            tests:
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_static.cpp::TestStatic.OperatorsAreDeclaredInTheHeaderAndRefinedInTheBody
          }
        }
        requirement REQ-00031-1 {
          tags: language, lld, class
          status: approved
          title: Interface, abstract and value shall be derived from the members, never written
          rationale: What is derived cannot contradict what is declared (R14).
          verification VER-00024-1 {
            title: Integration tests confirm interface, abstract and value are derived from the members, never written
            status: approved
            method: test
            tests:
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_static.cpp::TestStatic.InterfaceAndAbstractAreDerived
          }
        }
        requirement REQ-00032-2 {
          tags: language, lld, class
          status: approved
          title: Any entity or member shall open a body with fields, notes, annotations and nested artefacts, and a member's body with rules
          rationale:
            R8, R12, R13. Owner, 2026-11-07 (DS-94): the bracket contracts ([requires: ...]) are gone; what
            a member requires of its calls is a rule in its body, one syntax for one thing.
          verification VER-00025-2 {
            title: Integration tests confirm any entity or member opens a body with fields, notes and annotations, and no prose contract is kept
            status: approved
            method: test
            tests:
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_static.cpp::TestStatic.NotesLiveInMemberBodies
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_rules.cpp::TestRules.ABracketContractDoesNotParse
          }
        }
        requirement REQ-00101-1 {
          tags: language, lld, class
          status: approved
          title: A class shall declare its destructor as ~Name(), and an interface may have one
          text:
            A method named ~ and the class's name is its destructor (flag destructor). It is no
            part of the contract: like a constructor, it does not count against the derived
            interface stereotype, so an interface declares the virtual destructor the C++ guide
            asks of it.
          rationale: Found splitting the checker (DS-138, DS-143): IStep needs a virtual destructor and the language could not say it.
          verification VER-00110-1 {
            title: Integration tests confirm ~Name() is the destructor and an interface keeps its stereotype with one
            status: approved
            method: test
            tests:
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_destructors.cpp::TestDestructors.ATildeAndTheClassNameIsItsDestructor
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_destructors.cpp::TestDestructors.AnInterfaceKeepsItsDestructorAndStaysAnInterface
          }
        }
        requirement REQ-00033-1 {
          tags: language, lld, class
          status: approved
          title: An enum shall be a value type with its values, annotated like a class
          verification VER-00026-1 {
            title: Integration tests confirm an enum is a value type with its values, annotated like a class
            status: approved
            method: test
            tests:
              tests/integration/ds/bind/test_packages.cpp::TestPackages.AnEnumRealisesRequirementsLikeAClass
          }
        }
      }

      // ---- function ----
      requirement REQ-00063-1 {
        tags: language, lld, visibility
        status: approved
        title: Any child of a box may be private, and nothing outside its parent shall reach it
        text:
          One rule at every level: a box connects to another through a public child. A package's
          public children are its interfaces and modules, a module's its classes and functions, a
          class's its methods and attributes. A child is public unless it says -, and is seen from
          inside its parent, so siblings see each other. A call or a type that crosses anything
          private on its way down is W-NOT-VISIBLE; a public member showing a private type is
          W-PRIVATE-LEAK.
        rationale: Owner, 2026-11-05. There is no port concept: a port is a public child, and an interface is one that crosses a process. Whether the code respects this is argos's job.
        verification VER-00068-2 {
          title: Integration tests confirm any child of a box may be private, and nothing outside its parent reaches it
          status: approved
          method: test
          tests:
            tests/integration/ds/check/test_visibility.cpp::TestVisibility.AnyChildMayBePrivateAndIsPublicUnlessItSaysSo
            tests/integration/ds/check/test_visibility.cpp::TestVisibility.APrivateModuleIsNotReachedFromAnotherBox
            tests/integration/ds/check/test_visibility.cpp::TestVisibility.APrivateClassIsNotReachedFromAnotherModule
            tests/integration/ds/check/test_visibility.cpp::TestVisibility.APrivateMethodIsNotCalledFromAnotherClass
            tests/integration/ds/check/test_visibility.cpp::TestVisibility.APrivateFunctionIsNotCalledFromAnotherBox
            tests/integration/ds/check/test_visibility.cpp::TestVisibility.SiblingsSeeEachOther
            tests/integration/ds/check/test_visibility.cpp::TestVisibility.EveryOtherCrossingIsReportedExactlyAsMarked
            tests/integration/ds/check/test_visibility.cpp::TestVisibility.APublicMemberThatShowsAPrivateTypeIsALeak
            tests/integration/ds/check/test_visibility.cpp::TestVisibilityAlone.APublicOperatorThatShowsAPrivateTypeIsALeak
        }
      }
      requirement REQ-00054-1 {
        status: approved
        tags: language, lld, function
        verification VER-00058-1 {
          title: Unit tests confirm a function is an operation of its module: the functions oracle
          method: test
          tests:
            tests/integration/ds/check/test_functions.cpp::TestFunctions.TheOracleFindingsAndNothingElse
        }
        title: A function shall be an operation of a module, outside any class, identified by its module and its name
        text:
          function name(params) -> type in a module, with a member's optional
          visibility in front, public when absent; two of one name are
          E-DUPLICATE-IDENTITY. An extern module declares functions as names.
        rationale:
          A Python module or a C++ namespace declares operations no class
          holds; a design that wraps them in a class the code does not have
          drifts from it. Migrating iris (2026-10-26) found 133 of its design
          entities were functions.

        requirement REQ-00055-2 {

          status: approved
          tags: language, lld, function
          title: A function shall carry a method's signature and body
          text: Parameters and the return give use; the body holds notes, annotations, rules and nested artefacts.
          verification VER-00059-1 {
            title: Integration tests confirm a function carries a method's signature and body
            method: test
            tests:
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_functions.cpp::TestFunctions.AFunctionIsAnOperationOfItsModule
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_functions.cpp::TestFunctions.ItsSignatureGivesUseAndItsBodyIsAMethods
          }
        }
        requirement REQ-00056-1 {
          status: approved
          tags: language, lld, function
          title: The behaviour of a function shall run on its parameters and locals, and a call with no target shall reach a function of the module
          text:
            sequence gather { }; there is no self. A call with no target is a
            function resolved outward from the module, `-> tasks::gather()` one
            of another module; a method reaches one its class does not declare.
            In a sequence diagram a function runs on its module's lifeline.
          verification VER-00060-1 {
            title: Integration tests confirm the behaviour of a function runs on its parameters and locals, and a call with no target reaches a function of the module
            method: test
            tests:
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_functions.cpp::TestFunctions.ItsBehaviourRunsOnItsParametersAndCallsItsNeighbours
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_functions.cpp::TestFunctions.ASequenceOfAFunctionRunsOnItsModule
          }
        }
        requirement REQ-00057-1 {
          status: approved
          tags: language, lld, function
          title: A class diagram shall draw each function as a box of its own, stereotyped function
          verification VER-00061-1 {
            title: Integration tests confirm a class diagram draws each function as a box of its own, stereotyped function
            method: test
            tests:
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_functions.cpp::TestFunctions.AClassDiagramDrawsEachFunctionAsABox
          }
        }
      }

      // ---- sequence ----
      requirement REQ-00034-1 {
        tags: language, lld, sequence
        status: approved
        verification VER-00054-1 {
          status: approved
          title: Unit tests confirm a sequence is the behaviour of a method: the behaviour oracle
          method: test
          tests:
            tests/integration/ds/check/test_behaviour.cpp::TestBehaviour.TheOracleFindings
        }
        title: A sequence shall be the behaviour of a method, identified by it
        rationale: block 3, 2026-10-25.

        requirement REQ-00035-1 {
          tags: language, lld, sequence
          status: approved
          title: A sequence shall be identified by its resolved subject and scenario, wherever it is written
          text: sequence Class::method [/ scenario]; two declarations are a duplicate; the unnamed scenario is the default.
          verification VER-00027-1 {
            title: Integration tests confirm a sequence is identified by its resolved subject and scenario, wherever it is written
            status: approved
            method: test
            tests:
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_behaviour.cpp::TestBehaviour.ABehaviourIsIdentifiedByItsSubject
          }
        }
        requirement REQ-00036-2 {
          tags: language, lld, sequence
          status: approved
          title: The participants of a sequence shall be its static context: self, the attributes, the parameters, the locals written and the results of earlier messages
          rationale: Revision 2 adds the results (DS-51): a call on what an earlier message returned is an ordinary design, and it read as an undeclared participant.
          verification VER-00028-5 {
            title: Integration tests confirm the participants of a sequence are its static context: self, the attributes, the parameters, the locals written and the results of earlier messages, scoped as the code scopes them
            status: approved
            text:
              Revision 5 adds how a name resolves when two of them share it (DDEV-1242): a local
              hides a member of its name, a method is no value a message is sent to, and a result
              named like an attribute is stored in that attribute.
            method: test
            tests:
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_values.cpp::TestNameScopes.ALocalHidesAMemberOfItsNameAndAResultIsStoredInTheAttributeOfItsName
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_values.cpp::TestValues.ALocalInsideAFrameIsALocal
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_behaviour.cpp::TestBehaviour.ParticipantsComeFromTheStaticContext
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_values.cpp::TestValues.AResultIsAParticipantOfTheMessagesAfterIt
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_values.cpp::TestValues.AResultDoesNotExistBeforeItsMessage
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_inherited_members.cpp::TestInheritedMembers.ASelfCallReachesAMethodTheClassInherits
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_inherited_members.cpp::TestInheritedMembers.AnInheritedAttributeIsAParticipant
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_inherited_members.cpp::TestInheritedMembers.ACallOnASubclassReachesTheMethodOfItsBase
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_inherited_members.cpp::TestInheritedMembers.APrivateMemberOfTheBaseStaysHidden
          }
        }
        requirement REQ-00059-1 {
          tags: language, lld, sequence
          status: approved
          title: A behaviour shall say what it gives back with return, and that value shall be checked against what its operation declares
          text:
            return takes a name or a literal, never an expression. Its type is checked
            against the return of the operation (W-RETURN-TYPE), and an operation that
            returns none gives nothing back. A name the context does not know is left
            alone, as an argument is. An operation that declares no return has nothing
            to check against.
          rationale: DS-52. With the scenario a call follows, a trace reaches the value it ends in, which is what lets an interface promise an outcome.
          verification VER-00063-1 {
            title: Integration tests confirm a behaviour says what it gives back with return, and that value is checked against what its operation declares
            status: approved
            method: test
            tests:
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_scenarios.cpp::TestScenarios.AReturnIsCheckedAgainstWhatTheOperationDeclares
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_scenarios.cpp::TestScenarios.AReturnThatAgreesIsNotAFinding
          }
        }
        requirement REQ-00060-1 {
          tags: language, lld, sequence, interface
          status: approved
          title: An operation of an interface shall have a sequence, and each outcome it promises shall name a scenario whose trace ends in that value
          text:
            sequence shell::buy / refused goes down through the scenario each call names.
            An operation with no sequence is W-OPERATION-NO-BEHAVIOUR, an outcome naming no
            scenario W-SCENARIO-UNDECLARED, and one whose trace ends in another value
            W-OUTCOME-MISMATCH. What cannot be told, a value that is not a literal at the end
            of the trace, gives no finding.
          rationale: DS-54. This is the link from the high level design to the low level one, and what keeps a promise such as exit 2 true.
          verification VER-00065-1 {
            title: Integration tests confirm an operation of an interface has a sequence, and each outcome it promises names a scenario whose trace ends in that value
            status: approved
            method: test
            tests:
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_interfaces.cpp::TestInterfaces.AnOperationIsTheSubjectOfItsSequenceAndItsTraceGoesDown
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_interfaces.cpp::TestInterfaces.AnOperationWithNoSequenceIsAFinding
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_interfaces.cpp::TestInterfaces.AnOutcomeThatNamesNoScenarioIsAFinding
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_interfaces.cpp::TestInterfaces.AnOutcomeIsCheckedAgainstTheValueItsTraceEndsIn
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_interfaces.cpp::TestInterfaces.TheSequenceOfAnOperationIsDrawnDownThroughItsScenario
          }
        }
        requirement REQ-00061-1 {
          tags: language, lld, state, interface
          status: approved
          title: The state machine of an interface shall be its navigation, with views as its states, and shall report the views with no way in or out
          text:
            state web { view Home { text: ... } Home -> Done on buy }. A view holds free text and
            the requirements and constraints that bind it, nothing that reinvents HTML. An event
            that names an operation goes down to it; any other is a label. W-VIEW-UNDECLARED,
            W-VIEW-UNREACHABLE and W-VIEW-NO-WAY-OUT. Views are optional: a bare machine asks nothing.
          rationale: Owner, 2026-11-05. In a graphical interface the navigation is the design; the look is a requirement or a constraint.
          verification VER-00066-1 {
            title: Integration tests confirm the state machine of an interface is its navigation, with views as its states, and reports the views with no way in or out
            status: approved
            method: test
            tests:
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_interfaces.cpp::TestInterfaces.AViewIsAStateWithItsTextAndWhatBindsIt
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_interfaces.cpp::TestInterfaces.AnEventThatNamesAnOperationGoesDownAndAnyOtherIsALabel
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_interfaces.cpp::TestInterfaces.TheNavigationReportsViewsWithNoWayInOrOut
          }
        }
        requirement REQ-00065-1 {
          tags: language, lld, sequence
          status: approved
          title: A branch of a sequence shall name a scenario, a path through that one behaviour, so what scenarios share is written once
          text:
            opt <prose> / refused { ... return 2 } names a branch; a bare return ends it. The path of a
            scenario takes what is shared and its own branch, up to the return that ends it; the default
            path takes no named branch; of an alt with one named side, the other side is taken; a branch it
            cannot tell is kept as a frame. A call, a diagram and an exit code ask for the path by its
            name, as they do for a sequence of its own, which stays for paths that share nothing. A name
            given twice is W-SCENARIO-TWICE. A behaviour asked for by its subject is drawn whole, its early
            returns included; an unnamed call follows the default path.
          rationale: Owner, 2026-11-05. Repeating the opening of every scenario was the largest cost of the design of ds, and a maintenance risk. checkMessage went from twelve sequences to one.
          verification VER-00070-2 {
            title: Integration tests confirm a branch of a sequence names a scenario, a path through that one behaviour, so what scenarios share is written once
            status: approved
            method: test
            tests:
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_branches.cpp::TestBranches.ADiagramThatAsksForAScenarioNobodyDeclaresIsAFinding
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_branches.cpp::TestBranches.ABranchNamesAScenarioAndABareReturnEndsIt
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_branches.cpp::TestBranches.APathTakesWhatIsSharedAndItsBranchUpToItsReturn
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_branches.cpp::TestBranches.TheDefaultPathTakesNoNamedBranch
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_branches.cpp::TestBranches.ACallThatNamesABranchEntersThatPath
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_branches.cpp::TestBranches.AnExitCodeIsCheckedAgainstTheEndOfItsPath
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_branches.cpp::TestBranches.ANameGivenTwiceIsAFinding
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_branches.cpp::TestBranches.ABehaviourAskedForByItsSubjectIsDrawnWholeWithItsEarlyReturns
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_branches.cpp::TestBranches.AScenarioIsDrawnAsItsPathWithoutTheBranchesItSkips
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_branches.cpp::TestBranches.AnUnnamedCallFollowsTheDefaultPath
          }
        }
        requirement REQ-00110-1 {
          tags: language, lld, sequence, failure
          status: approved
          title: A sequence shall say where a path ends failing and where a failure of what it calls is handled, whatever the mechanism
          text:
            fail ParseError ends a path where a return would go, with the failure's name as text, as a
            type is written. attempt { ... } on IoError / unreadable { ... } runs its steps and handles
            what they fail with, one on each: a handler that fails with another translates the failure,
            one that returns resolves it, and a failure no handler names goes on to the caller. The
            default path does not fail: it takes the attempt's steps and no handler; a handler that
            names a scenario is the path of that failure. The diagram draws the failure and each handler.
          rationale: Owner, 2026-11-13 (DS-180, DS-187). One model of failure for exceptions, error values and error codes; what escapes each operation is computed from where failures start and where they are handled (DS-188).
          verification VER-00126-2 {
            title: Integration tests confirm a path ends failing with its failure's name, an attempt runs on every path and a handler only on the path that names it, and the diagram draws both
            status: approved
            text: Revision 2 (DS-189) holds the example to reporting only the failures its signatures misstate, now that it has some.
            method: test
            tests:
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_failures.cpp::TestFailures.TheExampleReportsNothingButTheFailuresItsSignaturesMisstate
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_failures.cpp::TestFailures.APathThatFailsEndsThereWithTheFailuresName
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_failures.cpp::TestFailures.AnAttemptRunsOnEveryPathAndAHandlerOnlyOnThePathThatNamesIt
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_failures.cpp::TestFailures.AHandlerKeepsTheFailureItHandles
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_failures.cpp::TestFailures.TheSequenceDiagramDrawsTheFailureAndTheHandlers
          }
        }
        requirement REQ-00111-1 {
          tags: language, lld, sequence, failure, check, query
          status: approved
          title: The checker shall compute what failures escape each operation, with the path each comes up by, and the query shall answer it
          text:
            A failure starts where a path ends failing and goes up to every caller that does not handle
            it: an attempt handles, around the steps it runs, what its handlers name; a handler's own
            steps are not handled by its attempt. Computed until nothing changes, so calls that call
            each other end. Each operation carries escapes, the failures, and escape.<failure>, the
            operations it comes up through and the behaviour (or the scenario of one) that starts it.
            A call ds cannot follow, to an operation with no behaviour, is taken not to fail.
            ds query <workspace> failures <operation> answers each escaping failure, named by the
            operation it starts in.
          rationale: Owner, 2026-11-13 (DS-180, DS-188). The design writes only where a failure starts and where it is handled; what escapes is inferred, for exceptions, error values and codes alike.
          verification VER-00127-2 {
            title: Tests confirm a failure escapes every caller that does not handle it, with its path and the scenario it starts in, that a handler's own failure goes on, that calls calling each other end, and that the query answers it
            status: approved
            method: test
            tests:
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_failures.cpp::TestFailures.AFailureEscapesEveryCallerThatDoesNotHandleIt
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_failures.cpp::TestFailures.EachEscapeKeepsThePathItComesUpByAndTheScenarioItStartsIn
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_failures.cpp::TestFailures.TheQueryAnswersWhatEscapesAnOperationByWhereEachStarts
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_failure_escapes.cpp::TestFailureEscapes.AFailureInsideAnAttemptThatHandlesItEscapesNothing
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_failure_escapes.cpp::TestFailureEscapes.AHandlersOwnFailureIsNotHandledByTheAttemptThatHoldsIt
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_failure_escapes.cpp::TestFailureEscapes.CallsThatCallEachOtherEndWithWhatEitherLetsEscape
          }
        }
        requirement REQ-00112-1 {
          tags: language, lld, failure, check
          status: approved
          title: A signature shall say what an operation may fail with, and the checker shall hold it to what escapes, and a boundary to saying it
          text:
            + load(path: string) -> Book fails LoadError, ParseError promises what may escape; fails
            nothing promises none. What escapes and the signature does not say is W-FAILURE-UNDECLARED;
            what it says and no path of its behaviour fails with is W-FAILURE-UNREACHED. An interface
            operation is a boundary: what escapes it is said in its signature, or nothing may. Any other
            operation is held to its signature only when it writes one. An operation with no behaviour
            fails as its signature says, so a call into a library can be said to fail.
          rationale: Owner, 2026-11-13 (DS-180, DS-189). noexcept is the promise that nothing escapes, decided per operation by the design, not by a rule over every method.
          verification VER-00128-1 {
            title: Tests confirm a signature is held to what escapes, a boundary says what escapes it, and an operation with no behaviour fails as its signature says
            status: approved
            method: test
            tests:
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_failures.cpp::TestFailurePromises.WhatEscapesAndTheSignatureDoesNotSayIsAFinding
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_failures.cpp::TestFailurePromises.WhatTheSignatureSaysAndNoPathFailsWithIsAFinding
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_failures.cpp::TestFailurePromises.AnOperationWithNoBehaviourFailsAsItsSignatureSays
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_failures.cpp::TestFailurePromises.ABoundarySaysWhatEscapesItOrNothingMay
          }
        }
        requirement REQ-00058-2 {
          tags: language, lld, sequence
          status: approved
          title: A value of a sequence shall have the type of what produced it, and its uses shall be checked against that type
          text:
            The result of a message has the type its operation returns. A call on a
            result is checked as a call on any other participant, an argument against
            the type of its parameter (W-ARG-TYPE), and taking the result of an operation
            that returns none is reported (W-RESULT-NONE). An argument may be a literal, a number or a
            string, and has the type it is written in. A value whose type is not
            known, because its operation declares no return or does not resolve, has
            nothing to be checked against and gives no finding.
          rationale: DS-51; revision 2 adds literal arguments (DS-64): the code passes them, and naming them invented values. Static and dynamic joined only by name and arity, so a sequence could not say anything about what flows through it.
          verification VER-00062-2 {
            title: Integration tests confirm a value of a sequence has the type of what produced it, and its uses are checked against that type
            status: approved
            method: test
            tests:
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_values.cpp::TestValues.ALiteralArgumentHasTheTypeItIsWrittenIn
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_values.cpp::TestValues.ACallOnAResultIsCheckedAgainstItsType
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_values.cpp::TestValues.AValueOfUnknownTypeHasNothingToBeCheckedAgainst
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_values.cpp::TestValues.AnArgumentOfTheWrongTypeIsReported
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_values.cpp::TestValues.ADerivedClassSatisfiesItsBaseAsAnArgument
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_values.cpp::TestValues.ATemplateWithCommasIsOneParameter
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_values.cpp::TestValues.TakingTheResultOfAnOperationThatReturnsNothingIsReported
          }
        }
        requirement REQ-00037-1 {
          tags: language, lld, sequence
          status: approved
          title: A message shall name an operation of its target's type and match its arity, inside loop, alt and opt frames with prose conditions
          verification VER-00029-2 {
            title: Integration tests confirm a message names an operation of its target's type and matches its arity, inside loop, alt and opt frames with prose conditions, each step held by what encloses it
            status: approved
            method: test
            tests:
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_behaviour.cpp::TestBehaviour.AnAltHoldsItsSidesAsBranchesAndEachSideItsSteps
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_checker.cpp::TestChecker.MessagesToExpectedTypesAreNotReportedTwice
          }
        }
        requirement REQ-00108-1 {
          tags: language, lld, sequence
          status: approved
          title: A message shall call a class's static operation by its qualified name, with no instance
          text:
            `-> diff::Diff::compare(a, b)`: a message with no participant whose qualified name
            names an operation of a class calls it on the class itself, as `-> tasks::gather(x)`
            calls a function of another module. The operation must be static; one that is not
            is W-MSG-NOT-STATIC, since it needs an instance: a local, an attribute or a parameter.
          rationale:
            DS-60 (Owner, 2026-11-13): Diff::compare is static, and a sequence could only call
            through a participant, so the design declared a local the code does not have.
          verification VER-00124-1 {
            title: Integration tests confirm a method's and a function's behaviour call a static operation on its class, and one that is not static is reported
            status: approved
            method: test
            tests:
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_static_calls.cpp::TestStaticCalls.AMethodsBehaviourCallsAStaticOperationOnItsClass
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_static_calls.cpp::TestStaticCalls.AFunctionsBehaviourCallsAStaticOperationOnItsClass
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_static_calls.cpp::TestStaticCalls.AnOperationThatIsNotStaticNeedsAnInstance
          }
        }
        requirement REQ-00038-2 {
          tags: language, lld, sequence
          status: approved
          title: A message to an operation with a behaviour shall expand to its default scenario or to the one it names, and coupling to another module shall be derived
          text:
            A call names a scenario as a declaration does, with a slash, and a scenario
            the operation does not declare is W-SCENARIO-UNDECLARED. Revision 2 adds the
            naming (DS-52): a trace could only go down through the default scenario.
          verification VER-00030-2 {
            title: Integration tests confirm a message to an operation with a behaviour expands to its default scenario or to the one it names, and coupling to another module is derived
            status: approved
            method: test
            tests:
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_scenarios.cpp::TestScenarios.ACallThatNamesAScenarioExpandsToThatOne
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_scenarios.cpp::TestScenarios.ACallThatNamesNoScenarioExpandsToTheDefault
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_scenarios.cpp::TestScenarios.AScenarioNobodyDeclaresIsAFinding
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_behaviour.cpp::TestBehaviour.AMessageToAnOperationWithABehaviourExpandsToIt
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_behaviour.cpp::TestBehaviour.CouplingIsDerivedFromWhatABehaviourTouchesOutsideItsModule
          }
        }
      }

      // ---- state ----
      requirement REQ-00039-1 {
        tags: language, lld, state
        status: approved
        verification VER-00055-1 {
          status: approved
          title: Unit tests confirm a state machine is the behaviour of a class
          method: test
          tests:
            tests/integration/ds/check/test_behaviour.cpp::TestBehaviour.StateEventsAndActionsAreOperations
        }
        title: A state machine shall be the behaviour of a class
        rationale: block 3, 2026-10-25.

        requirement REQ-00040-1 {
          tags: language, lld, state
          status: approved
          title: The events and actions of a transition shall be operations of the class, and the guard shall be prose
          text: Idle -> Running on run [guard] / report; no nested states until a design asks for them.
          verification VER-00031-1 {
            title: Integration tests confirm the events and actions of a transition are operations of the class, and the guard is prose
            status: approved
            method: test
            tests:
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_behaviour.cpp::TestBehaviour.StateEventsAndActionsAreOperations
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_checker.cpp::TestChecker.AStateEventMustBeAnOperationOfItsEntity
          }
        }

        requirement REQ-00109-1 {
          tags: language, lld, state, check
          status: approved
          title: The checker shall report a state of a class's machine that no transition leads to from its initial state
          text:
            A state named in the transitions that the walk from the initial state never enters is
            W-STATE-UNREACHABLE: a state left over, or a transition missing. A machine with no initial
            state written says nothing, since where it starts cannot be told. The navigation of an
            interface has its own (W-VIEW-UNREACHABLE).
          rationale: DS-53, measured 2026-11-05: `Lost -> Idle on go`, never entered, passed silently.
          verification VER-00125-1 {
            title: Integration tests confirm a state nothing leads to from the initial one is reported, and a machine fully reached or with no initial state says nothing
            status: approved
            method: test
            tests:
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_behaviour.cpp::TestStateReach.AStateNothingLeadsToFromTheInitialOneIsAFinding
              tests/integration/ds/check/test_behaviour.cpp::TestStateReach.AMachineEveryStateOfWhichIsReachedOrWithNoInitialStateSaysNothing
          }
        }
      }

      // ---- activity ----
      requirement REQ-00041-1 {
        tags: language, lld, activity
        title: An activity shall be the behaviour of a process
        text: Reserved: nothing is decided until the process domain arrives.
      }
    }

    // ======================= logic ========================================
    requirement REQ-00095-2 {
      tags: language, logic, rules
      status: approved
      title: The language shall declare rules and definitions in the box they apply to, in a formal syntax: what they speak about, which of them, and what holds, answering to a requirement
      text:
        rule <name> { @requirement <ID>; for <kind> <variable> [in <box>], ...; where <literals>;
        holds <literals> | never <literals> } in a package, a module, a class or a member;
        definition <name>(<parameters>) { if <literals> ... } names a relation derived from others,
        one case per if line. A literal is a relation of the metamodel (c uses x), a kind (x is
        class), containment (x in p@core), a comparison (=, !=, <, <=, >, >=) of entities or values,
        a definition applied (reaches(c, x)) or the literal argument of a call (arg(k, msg, v)),
        negated by not; a bare name is a variable, an entity is written qualified and a value is a
        number or a string. What a rule
        says is read from this syntax and never from prose: holds: <words> does not parse. A rule
        is a design piece with a name, not an artefact with a revision: it makes a requirement real
        in a narrower context and may name the entities of the design, which a requirement does not.
        A rule that answers to no requirement, or says no claim or more than one, and a definition
        with no case, are findings.
      rationale:
        Owner, 2026-11-07 (DS-94): the logic perspective of a design, beside its structure and its
        behaviour; constraints that spoke about the design and design rules hidden in comments get a
        place where they can be checked.
      verification VER-00104-2 {
        title: Integration tests confirm rules and definitions are declared in the box they apply to, link to their requirement, and the ones that say nothing are reported
        status: approved
        method: test
        tests:
          tests/integration/ds/check/test_rules.cpp::TestRules.ARuleIsADesignPieceInTheBoxItAppliesTo
          tests/integration/ds/check/test_rules.cpp::TestRules.ADefinitionIsARelationWithTheCasesInWhichItHolds
          tests/integration/ds/check/test_rules.cpp::TestRules.ARuleThatAnswersToNothingOrClaimsNothingIsReported
          tests/integration/ds/check/test_rules.cpp::TestRules.ProseIsNotARule
          tests/integration/ds/check/test_rules.cpp::TestRules.ARuleOfAMemberIsNamedUnderIt
          tests/integration/ds/check/test_rules.cpp::TestRules.RuleAndDefinitionStayNamesWhereANameIsExpected
      }
    }

    requirement REQ-00117-1 {
      tags: language, logic, rules, check
      status: approved
      title: A relation literal that binds an end to a kind the relation never joins there shall be reported as W-RULE-NEVER-MATCHES
      text:
        The kind of a variable is read from its range or from a positive kind literal, and the kind
        of an entity from the model. When a relation literal binds its source to a kind the relation
        never leaves, or its target to a kind it never reaches, by the metamodel, the literal matches
        nothing: the rule is decided by vacuity. It is a warning at the literal; the rule is still
        evaluated.
      rationale:
        Model audit 2026-11, finding G1 (DS-213): for class c ... never c uses x could never be
        broken, since uses leaves members and never a class, and it was the example of ds manual
        rule. A vacuous rule stands as the verification of a requirement and is always green. The
        manual's example now speaks about the members.
      verification VER-00133-1 {
        status: approved
        title: Integration tests confirm a literal that can never match is reported and the member-level rule is broken where the design breaks it
        method: test
        tests:
          tests/integration/ds/check/test_rules.cpp::TestRules.ALiteralThatCanNeverMatchIsReported
      }
    }

    requirement REQ-00096-1 {
      tags: language, logic, rules, check
      status: approved
      title: The checker shall decide every structural rule over the model and report each binding of its ranges that breaks it
      text:
        Rules are evaluated as Datalog with stratified negation over the model: the facts are the
        declared entities with their kinds, every relation of the metamodel and containment at any
        depth. A definition is computed to its fixpoint, recursion included; a rule's holds is broken
        by each binding of its ranges and where that has no answer, its never by each binding that
        has one, reported with the binding and the answer (E-RULE-BROKEN). The model is finite, so
        every rule is decided. A formula that names an unknown kind, relation, entity or definition
        (E-RULE-UNKNOWN), applies a definition to the wrong number of arguments (E-RULE-ARITY),
        tests a variable no positive literal binds (E-RULE-UNSAFE) or negates a definition through
        its own recursion (E-RULE-UNSTRATIFIED) is reported and not evaluated.
      rationale:
        Owner, 2026-11-07 (DS-94): structural rules are always decidable in the design, in a formal
        or semi-formal syntax; nothing is inferred from prose or keywords. Rules about behaviour wait
        for contracts and recorded runs.
      verification VER-00105-3 {
        title: Integration tests confirm rules are decided over the model, broken bindings are reported with their answer, malformed or undecidable formulas are rejected, and the rules of a file that stops parsing are decided to the end
        status: approved
        method: test
        tests:
          tests/integration/ds/check/test_rule_evaluation.cpp::TestRuleEvaluation.ARuleIsBrokenByEveryBindingThatBreaksIt
          tests/integration/ds/check/test_rule_evaluation.cpp::TestRuleEvaluation.ANegationTestsWhatIsAlreadyBound
          tests/integration/ds/check/test_rule_evaluation.cpp::TestRuleEvaluation.ADefinitionRecursUntilItsFixpoint
          tests/integration/ds/check/test_rule_evaluation.cpp::TestRuleEvaluation.WhatARuleNamesMustExistAndItsVariablesBeBound
          tests/integration/ds/check/test_rule_evaluation.cpp::TestRuleEvaluation.ANegationThroughRecursionIsRejected
          tests/integration/ds/check/test_half_typed.cpp::TestHalfTypedFile.TheRulesOfAFileThatStopsParsingAreDecidedAndTheCheckEnds
          tests/integration/ds/check/test_half_typed.cpp::TestHalfTypedFile.TheSameRulesAreDecidedOnceTheFileParses
      }
    }

    requirement REQ-00097-1 {
      tags: language, logic, rules, check, sequence
      status: approved
      title: The checker shall decide the rules over the calls of the sequences against the literal arguments they pass, and report each call that breaks one where the call is written
      text:
        A call of a sequence is a message entity that calls an operation; arg(k, p, v) holds when
        the call k passes to the parameter p of what it calls a value v written as a literal in the
        sequence, a number or a string. Values compare numbers as numbers and anything else as
        written. A call that passes a name instead of a literal has no arg fact for that parameter,
        so a rule that asks for one in its where leaves it out: undecided in the design, it is
        neither kept nor broken. A broken rule is reported at the first thing it ranges over, the
        call in its sequence.
      rationale:
        Owner, 2026-11-07 (DS-94): contracts are rules too, with the rule's syntax; brackets gone,
        one syntax for one thing.
      verification VER-00106-1 {
        title: Integration tests confirm rules over calls are decided against their literal arguments, calls passing names are left out, and the finding sits on the call
        status: approved
        method: test
        tests:
          tests/integration/ds/check/test_rule_evaluation.cpp::TestRuleEvaluation.ARuleOfAMemberIsKeptOrBrokenByTheLiteralsItsCallsPass
          tests/integration/ds/check/test_rule_evaluation.cpp::TestRuleEvaluation.ValuesCompareNumbersAsNumbersAndTheRestAsWritten
      }
    }

    requirement REQ-00098-1 {
      tags: logic, rules, check, export
      status: approved
      title: The engine shall keep every binding that breaks a rule, with its answer and where it lands, and hand it structured to the export and to pyds
      text:
        Each breach the evaluator finds is kept by the rule's identity: the variables of its ranges
        and where as bound, for a never the answer that breaks it, and the location of the first
        thing the rule ranges over. All of them are kept, although the findings stop at a few per
        rule. The JSON export carries them under breaches, and pyds loads them as Model.breaches, so
        a reader lights what breaks a rule without reading the findings' prose.
      rationale:
        Owner, 2026-11-09 (DS-108): the rules must be seen to be understood; the prototype read the
        findings' messages, which is no contract.
      verification VER-00107-1 {
        title: Tests confirm every breach is kept with its bindings, its answer and where it lands, and travels structured through the export and pyds
        status: approved
        method: test
        tests:
          tests/integration/ds/check/test_rule_evaluation.cpp::TestRuleEvaluation.EveryBreachIsKeptWithItsBindingsItsAnswerAndWhereItLands
          tests/integration/python/test_pyds.py::TestRules::test_what_breaks_a_rule_comes_with_its_bindings_and_its_answer
      }
    }

    // ======================= artefacts ====================================
    requirement REQ-00042-1 {
      tags: language, artefacts
      status: approved
      verification VER-00056-1 {
        status: approved
        title: Unit tests confirm artefacts are held in the same model: the artefacts oracle
        method: test
        tests:
          tests/integration/ds/check/test_artefacts.cpp::TestArtefacts.TheOracleFindingsAndNothingElse
      }
      title: The language shall hold requirements, constraints and verifications as artefacts of the same model
      rationale: block 1, 2026-10-25.

      requirement REQ-00043-1 {
        tags: language, artefacts
        status: approved
        title: An artefact shall be identified by its id with its revision
        text: REQ-00001-2: the revision is part of the identity; a link to a revision no longer declared is W-REVISION-DRIFT, resolved to the declared one.
        verification VER-00032-2 {
          title: Integration tests confirm an artefact is identified by its id with its revision
          status: approved
          method: test
          tests:
            tests/integration/ds/check/test_artefacts.cpp::TestArtefacts.TheRevisionIsPartOfTheIdentityAndLinksNameIt
            tests/integration/ds/check/test_usecase_links.cpp::TestUseCaseLinks.ARealisationBehindTheRevisionIsReportedAndFollowsIt
            tests/integration/ds/check/test_usecase_links.cpp::TestUseCaseLinks.ASpecialisationThatNamesNoRevisionIsUnpinned
            tests/integration/ds/check/test_usecase_links.cpp::TestUseCaseLinksAlone.AUseCaseNobodyDeclaresIsSaidOnce
        }
        constraint CST-00006-1 {
          tags: language, artefacts
          status: approved
          category: language
          title: Every link to an artefact shall name a revision
          text: An unpinned link is E-REF-UNPINNED.
          rationale: Pinning links to a revision is what lets the tool tell who stayed behind when an artefact moved (block 1).
        }
      }
      requirement REQ-00044-1 {
        tags: language, artefacts
        status: approved
        title: Nesting shall give the relation between artefacts, and annotations shall add relations from elsewhere
        text: a requirement in a requirement refines it; a verification in a requirement verifies it; @refines, @requirement, @constraint elsewhere.
        verification VER-00033-1 {
          title: Integration tests confirm nesting gives the relation between artefacts, and annotations add relations from elsewhere
          status: approved
          method: test
          tests:
            tests/integration/ds/bind/test_binder.cpp::TestBinder.NestingGivesTheRelation
            tests/integration/ds/check/test_artefacts.cpp::TestArtefacts.LevelByPlacementAndNestingGivesTheRelation
            tests/integration/ds/check/test_artefacts.cpp::TestArtefacts.TheSeparateFileIsTheNormalPlace
        }
      }
      requirement REQ-00114-1 {
        tags: language, artefacts, annotations
        status: approved
        title: An annotation word the language gives no meaning to shall be reported as W-ANNOTATION-UNKNOWN
        text:
          A @word outside the table of annotations is a warning where it is written,
          naming the word and the words the language knows. The link it makes is kept
          (refers): the warning does not drop it, and loading never fails on it.
        rationale:
          Model audit 2026-11, finding G2 (DS-210): @requirment REQ-1 traced nothing and
          reported nothing, the easiest silent failure of the language and in its
          traceability. No design of the fleet uses a free annotation word.
        verification VER-00130-1 {
          status: approved
          title: Integration tests confirm an unknown annotation word is reported where it is written and its link is kept, and the artefacts corpus marks one
          method: test
          tests:
            tests/integration/ds/bind/test_binder.cpp::TestBinder.AnAnnotationWordTheLanguageDoesNotKnowIsReportedAndKept
            tests/integration/ds/check/test_artefacts.cpp::TestArtefacts.TheOracleFindingsAndNothingElse
        }
      }
      requirement REQ-00118-1 {
        tags: language, artefacts, static
        status: approved
        title: A cycle of refines or of inherits shall be an error, and a requirement that refines one written inside its own box shall be reported as W-REFINES-UPWARD
        text:
          Requirements that refine each other through any chain are E-REFINES-CYCLE; classes or
          use cases that derive from each other are E-INHERITANCE-CYCLE; each cycle is said once.
          A requirement whose refined requirement is written inside its own box, further down the
          containment axis, is a warning: the detail stands above what it details. The axis is
          read from where each is written, never from the prefix of its id.
        rationale:
          Model audit 2026-11, finding G10 (DS-214): only the ownership cycle was reported. A
          cycle is a contradiction between written things, not an absence. Reporting a
          requirement that nothing answers to stays out on purpose: that is absence (DS-216).
        verification VER-00134-1 {
          status: approved
          title: Integration tests confirm refines and inherits cycles are errors, a tree is not, and an upward refinement is reported while a downward one is not
          method: test
          tests:
            tests/integration/ds/check/test_cycles.cpp::TestCycles.RequirementsThatRefineEachOtherAreACycleAndTheUpwardOneIsSaid
            tests/integration/ds/check/test_cycles.cpp::TestCycles.ClassesThatDeriveFromEachOtherAreACycleAndATreeIsNot
            tests/integration/ds/check/test_cycles.cpp::TestCycles.ARequirementThatRefinesOneOfTheSystemIsNoFinding
        }
      }
      requirement REQ-00045-1 {
        tags: language, artefacts
        status: approved
        title: An artefact shall carry title, text, rationale, status and tags; a verification its method and tests; a constraint its category and bok
        text: One-line forms for a requirement and a constraint; draft when no status.
        verification VER-00034-1 {
          title: Integration tests confirm an artefact carries title, text, rationale, status and tags; a verification its method and tests; a constraint its category and bok
          status: approved
          method: test
          tests:
            tests/integration/ds/check/test_artefacts.cpp::TestArtefacts.FieldsAsDecided
            tests/integration/ds/check/test_static.cpp::TestStatic.ConstraintsAreArtefactsInBothForms
        }
      }
    }

    // ======================= diagrams =====================================
    requirement REQ-00047-1 {
      tags: language, diagrams
      status: approved
      verification VER-00057-1 {
        status: approved
        title: Unit tests confirm a diagram is a selection of the model
        method: test
        tests:
          tests/integration/ds/render/test_requirements_view.cpp::TestRequirementsView.ThePackageTreeWithoutDesign
          tests/integration/ds/render/test_text.cpp::TestText.DrawsEveryBoxWithItsNameAndMembers
      }
      title: A diagram shall be a selection of the model that decides what to print and never what to draw
      rationale: Keeping the views as selections keeps them from drifting.

      requirement REQ-00048-1 {
        tags: language, diagrams
        status: approved
        title: A diagram shall select by id, module or package, with include and exclude, and print by hide and show
        verification VER-00036-1 {
          title: Integration tests confirm a diagram selects by id, module or package, with include and exclude, and prints by hide and show
          status: approved
          method: test
          tests:
            tests/integration/ds/render/test_irexport.cpp::TestIrExport.ListsTheDeclaredDiagrams
            tests/integration/ds/render/test_irexport.cpp::TestIrExport.IncludeSelectsAndTheModuleBecomesAContainer
        }
      }
      requirement REQ-00116-1 {
        tags: language, diagrams
        status: approved
        title: A diagram pattern shall read the same in every kind of diagram, and one that names what nothing declares shall be reported as W-DIAGRAM-UNDECLARED
        text:
          include, exclude and open take an identity, a prefix with * over the identity or
          the scope (p@m::* is the module p@m and everything in it), a module named as such,
          or a template written without its arity, read alike by class, sequence, state and
          requirement diagrams. A pattern that names nothing the workspace declares is a
          warning at the diagram. A pattern over a box that exists and is empty is not: a
          level with no children is valid.
        rationale:
          Model audit 2026-11, findings G3 and I9 (DS-212): a diagram whose include named a
          class that had been moved drew less and said nothing, while the same broken
          reference in the model is a finding; p@m::* selected a module in a class diagram and
          nothing in a requirement diagram; package:x, documented, selected nothing anywhere.
          The check found two such diagrams in driftspec's own design.
        verification VER-00132-1 {
          status: approved
          title: Integration tests confirm a pattern that names nothing is reported and an empty box is not, and a requirement diagram reads a module pattern as a class diagram does
          method: test
          tests:
            tests/integration/ds/render/test_open_boxes.cpp::TestOpenBoxes.APatternThatNamesWhatNothingDeclaresIsAFinding
            tests/integration/ds/render/test_open_boxes.cpp::TestDiagramPatterns.ARequirementDiagramReadsAModulePatternAsAClassDiagramDoes
        }
      }
      requirement REQ-00049-2 {
        tags: language, diagrams
        status: approved
        title: A sequence diagram shall select a behaviour as it is written, expand by depth and lift to the level asked for
        verification VER-00037-4 {
          title: Integration tests confirm a sequence diagram selects a behaviour as it is written, expands by depth and lifts to the level asked for
          status: approved
          method: test
          tests:
            tests/integration/ds/check/test_values.cpp::TestValues.TwoObjectsOfOneTypeAreTwoLifelines
            tests/integration/ds/check/test_values.cpp::TestValues.AFrameWithNoMessageIsStillDrawn
            tests/integration/ds/render/test_open_boxes.cpp::TestOpenBoxes.DepthStarIsEveryLevelAndNeverAnAbort
            tests/integration/ds/render/test_open_boxes.cpp::TestOpenBoxes.ADepthThatIsNoNumberIsAFindingAndStillDraws
            tests/integration/ds/check/test_scenarios.cpp::TestScenarios.ASubjectAloneDrawsItsDefaultScenario
            tests/integration/ds/check/test_scenarios.cpp::TestScenarios.AScenarioIsSelectedAsItIsWrittenAndItsTraceFollowsIt
            tests/integration/ds/check/test_scenarios.cpp::TestScenarios.AStarSelectsEveryScenario
            tests/integration/ds/check/test_scenarios.cpp::TestScenarios.TheArrowBackCarriesWhatTheBehaviourReturns
            tests/integration/ds/check/test_behaviour.cpp::TestBehaviour.ASequenceDiagramExpandsByDepthAndLinksAtDepthZero
            tests/integration/ds/check/test_behaviour.cpp::TestBehaviour.LiftingToModuleLevelKeepsOnlyCrossModuleMessages
        }
      }
      requirement REQ-00064-2 {
        tags: language, diagrams, visibility
        status: approved
        title: A class diagram shall open the boxes it names and close the rest, each closed box showing only its public children
        text:
          open: shop@store@stock opens that box and the way to it; open: alone closes them all; a
          diagram that does not say open draws everything open. An edge that loses an end to a closed
          box says only that one box depends on the other, once, and what stays inside a closed box
          is not drawn. A behaviour that crosses boxes counts too, so an interface reaches what
          handles it though no type says so. The component view is derived, never written.
        rationale: Owner, 2026-11-05. Encapsulation has to be seen: which box holds what, and what each one offers.
        verification VER-00069-2 {
          title: Integration tests confirm a class diagram opens the boxes it names and closes the rest, each closed box showing only its public children
          status: approved
          method: test
          tests:
            tests/integration/ds/render/test_open_boxes.cpp::TestOpenBoxesBehaviour.ABehaviourThatCrossesBoxesIsAnEdgeOfTheClosedDrawing
            tests/integration/ds/render/test_open_boxes.cpp::TestOpenBoxes.OpenAloneClosesEveryBox
            tests/integration/ds/render/test_open_boxes.cpp::TestOpenBoxes.AClosedBoxShowsOnlyItsPublicChildren
            tests/integration/ds/render/test_open_boxes.cpp::TestOpenBoxes.EdgesLiftToTheBoxesThatAreSeenAndOnlyOnce
            tests/integration/ds/render/test_open_boxes.cpp::TestOpenBoxes.OpeningABoxShowsTheWayToItAndClosesTheRest
            tests/integration/ds/render/test_open_boxes.cpp::TestOpenBoxes.AnEdgeReachesInsideAnOpenBoxFromAClosedOne
            tests/integration/ds/render/test_open_boxes.cpp::TestOpenBoxes.ADiagramThatDoesNotSayOpenDrawsEverythingOpen
        }
      }
      requirement REQ-00062-1 {
        tags: language, diagrams, state
        status: approved
        title: A state diagram shall draw the states and the jumps of a machine, and of an interface its navigation with what each view shows
        text:
          diagram ST_Web { kind: state; include: shop@web }. It reads from the initial state down;
          a jump is an edge with its event and guard, a jump to the same state is a loop, and a view
          shows its text and what binds it. A view no jump names is still drawn.
        rationale: DS-5. In a graphical interface the navigation is the design, so it has to be seen.
        verification VER-00067-1 {
          title: Integration tests confirm a state diagram draws the states and the jumps of a machine, and of an interface its navigation with what each view shows
          status: approved
          method: test
          tests:
            tests/integration/ds/render/test_state_view.cpp::TestStateView.TheViewsAreBoxesWithWhatTheyShowAndWhatBindsThem
            tests/integration/ds/render/test_state_view.cpp::TestStateView.TheJumpsAreEdgesWithTheirEventAndGuard
            tests/integration/ds/render/test_state_view.cpp::TestStateView.TheMachineStartsFromItsInitialState
            tests/integration/ds/render/test_state_view.cpp::TestStateView.AViewNoJumpNamesIsStillDrawn
            tests/integration/ds/render/test_state_view.cpp::TestStateView.TheMachineOfAClassIsDrawnFromItsTransitionsAlone
            tests/integration/ds/render/test_state_view.cpp::TestSelfLoop.ARelationOfABoxWithItselfIsRoutedOutOfItsSideAndBack
        }
      }
      requirement REQ-00050-1 {
        tags: language, diagrams
        status: approved
        title: A requirement diagram shall show the umbrella of an artefact: what refines, verifies and realises it
        verification VER-00038-1 {
          title: Integration tests confirm a requirement diagram shows the umbrella of an artefact: what refines, verifies and realises it
          status: approved
          method: test
          tests:
            tests/integration/ds/render/test_requirements_view.cpp::TestRequirementsView.TheUmbrellaOfARequirement
            tests/integration/ds/render/test_requirements_view.cpp::TestRequirementsViewOfAUseCase.AUseCaseThatRealisesARequirementIsDrawnAsItsCard
        }
      }
    }

  }

